            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I had a similar problem with my first plugin, what I did was the following (in VimScript)\r\n```\r\n....\r\nlet empty_buffer_nr = bufnr(\"%\")\r\nexecute \":e \" . a:item\r\nexecute \":silent bd \" . empty_buffer_nr\r\n....\r\n```\r\nIn the first line I memorize the buffer number I'm \"using\" as a menu, open my file in edit mode and then silently do a buffer delete on the \"used buffer\"",
            "created_at": "2022-01-04T21:21:27Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/35#issuecomment-1005179428",
