        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should be fixed now in `main` branch.\r\n\r\nIssue was not exactly like you pointed (starter buffer not closing), but similar: it was a buffer created by Neovim on startup. As 'mini.starter' always created new buffer, that previous one was left untouched. I settled on allowing to open Starter in specified buffer and used this on startup to occupy initial empty buffer.",
            "created_at": "2022-01-06T14:17:58Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/35#issuecomment-1006625840",
